From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 13:10:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] cmake: request only Development.Module from FindPython

distribution.cmake asks FindPython for the full Development component,
which requires both Development.Module and Development.Embed (a libpython
usable for embedding). manylinux wheel-building images build CPython with
Py_ENABLE_SHARED=0 and ship no libpython at all (PEP 513), so
Development.Embed's Python_LIBRARIES lookup fails and configure aborts
with the "python3 development library ... need to be installed first"
error, even though _dearpygui only ever needs Development.Module (on
Linux it never links ${Python_LIBRARIES}). This is independent of
riscv64: it reproduces the same way in the x86_64/aarch64 manylinux
images; upstream's own Linux wheels avoid it only because they build
against actions/setup-python's shared-libpython interpreters outside
manylinux.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; this repo does not open issues/PRs on third-party repositories]

---
 src/distribution.cmake | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/distribution.cmake b/src/distribution.cmake
index c943053..01e98f5 100644
--- a/src/distribution.cmake
+++ b/src/distribution.cmake
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 cmake_minimum_required (VERSION 3.16)
 
-find_package (Python ${MV_PY_VERSION} EXACT COMPONENTS Development)
-if(NOT Python_Development_FOUND)
+find_package (Python ${MV_PY_VERSION} EXACT COMPONENTS Development.Module)
+if(NOT Python_Development.Module_FOUND)
 	message(FATAL_ERROR "The python3 development library from your distribution repo need to be installed first!")
 endif()
 
-- 
